00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,558
Teacher midterm practice, question 38.

2
00:00:04,178 --> 00:00:07,339
True or false: when molten metals solidify into

3
00:00:07,339 --> 00:00:11,243
crystals, they contain no vacancies or dislocations.

4
00:00:11,243 --> 00:00:16,015
These defects are only created when the solid is plastically deformed.

5
00:00:17,715 --> 00:00:22,983
Vacancies exist in equilibrium in every crystal above absolute zero.

6
00:00:22,983 --> 00:00:27,128
Their number is N times e to the minus Q v over k T.

7
00:00:27,748 --> 00:00:30,859
And dislocations form during solidification, and

8
00:00:30,859 --> 00:00:33,731
from thermal stresses as the metal cools.

9
00:00:33,731 --> 00:00:38,637
Plastic deformation multiplies them; it does not create the first ones.

10
00:00:40,236 --> 00:00:42,132
So the answer is B: false.

11
00:00:42,952 --> 00:00:45,483
Defects do not only come from deformation.

12
00:00:45,483 --> 00:00:47,290
Every real crystal has them.
